OL,3,AMicrosoft says services fully restored
OL,4,Aafter day-long global outage
OL,5,
OL,6,FMicrosoft has said its services have
OL,7,Fbeen fully restored after a worldwide
OL,8,Foutage affected several of its tools,
OL,9,Fcausing disruption.
OL,11,FThe tech firm said early on Saturday
OL,12,Fmorning that efforts to address the
OL,13,Funderlying problem had been completed
OL,14,Fand customers using Outlook, Teams and
OL,15,FCopilot should no longer be affected.
OL,17,FThe outage hit more than 70 countries,
OL,18,Fdisrupting everything from business
OL,19,Foperations to government services and
OL,20,Fpersonal users. More than 430 million
OL,21,Fpeople use the affected products
OL,22,Fworldwide.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,0,100
